# Slot 3 (Calibrated Confidence, Biology, excess, standard) — review log

## 2026-04-10 cycle 9 — fact pack curation

**Fact pack written:** `corpus/fact-packs/09-biology-songbird-decline-multi-cause-01.md`

**Scenario design rationale:** A ground-nesting songbird population decline study over 10 years across 40 sites, with three independent data sources (point counts, eBird, banding station) converging on a 32–38% decline estimate. The decline itself is strongly triangulated; the **cause** is not. Four candidate causes — habitat loss (18% reduction, directly measured), pesticides (tested at only 4 of 40 sites), climate-prey mismatch (r = 0.31, p = 0.08), and disease (unstudied) — have very different evidence strengths. The scenario is designed so a calibrated reasoner uses strong confidence for the decline estimate and differentiated moderate/weak confidence for the various cause candidates. The excess reasoner collapses the attribution into confident single-cause language (habitat loss = THE cause), flattening the asymmetric evidence.

